This is bad advice. Quantity of monsters isn't important in this case,
it's quality. If you're trying to appease an angry God, then you have
to find a sufficiently ugly monster to sacrifice. Someone has posted a
link to a list of suitable monsters elsethread. The easiest suitable
monster to find for a low-lovel character imho is a black pudding. They
are also relatively safe to kill, if you know their strengths and
weaknesses.

>    I frequently get 3 or 4 artifacts by donating at an altar on the
>    first or second level before I've even been to sokoban. You'll get
>    more food too from drops and corpses as you get weak.

No, the amount of food you get from corpses/ death drops in not
determined by how hungry you are. It depends solely on the size of the
monsters are that are generated, which in turns depends (more or less)
on the player's XP level and current dungeon level. Many low-level
monsters don't always leave a corpse. By the time you are tough
enough/deep enough that you can survive on randomly generated monsters
alone, you will likely have a huge stash of rations somewhere anyway.

> Only eat after you get weak and that way satiation won't be a problem

Satiation isn't generally as big a problem for low-level characters as
starvation. Eat every corpse that is safe to eat as soon as you kill it
(but don't eat when satiated, as chuckcar says). The only exceptions
are lichen and lizard corpses, which you can save for later.



